# Docs sync and style

- Docs mirror the code path: `src/a/b.js` is documented in `docs/src/a/b.js.md`.
- Before editing a code file, read its mirrored doc. After editing, fix stale parts and add missing information in the same commit.
- New code file needs a new doc. Deleted code file needs its doc deleted.
- Code style: minimal and readable. Multi-line comments only at the top of a file. Explanations belong in `docs/`.
- Run `npm run lint` and `npm test` before committing.

Full rules: `AGENTS.md` and `docs/guidelines.md`.
